Installation
------------

Ready-made packages are the easiest way to install paperman:

- Ubuntu: from the PPA

     sudo add-apt-repository ppa:sjg1/ppa
     sudo apt install paperman

- most Linux distributions: the snap

     sudo snap install paperman

- other Linux distributions: the AppImage, from the releases page
- Windows (x64 and Arm): the installer, from the releases page
- macOS (Apple Silicon and Intel): the disk image, from the releases page

The releases are at https://github.com/sjg20/paperman/releases and the
installation guide at https://paperman.readthedocs.io/en/latest/install.html


Building on Debian / Ubuntu
---------------------------

Paperman is built with Qt 6 and qmake. It needs:

- Qt 6: qmake6, qt6-base-dev, qt6-base-dev-tools, qt6-scxml-dev,
  qt6-svg-dev (for the icons) and libqt6sql6-sqlite (SQLite is used for
  the search index)
- libpoppler-qt6-dev, for showing PDFs
- libpodofo-dev, for writing PDFs (0.9, 0.10 and 1.x all work)
- libsane-dev, for scanning
- libtiff-dev, libjpeg-dev and zlib1g-dev

and, when it runs:

- tesseract-ocr, with a language such as tesseract-ocr-eng, to read the
  text of pages (OCR). Without it paperman works as usual but pages are
  not read, so they cannot be searched for by their text
- libimage-exiftool-perl, for keeping titles, notes and text in JPEG
  stacks

To install all of these:

   sudo apt install build-essential qmake6 qt6-base-dev qt6-base-dev-tools \
      qt6-scxml-dev qt6-svg-dev libqt6sql6-sqlite libpoppler-qt6-dev \
      libpodofo-dev libsane-dev libtiff-dev libjpeg-dev zlib1g-dev \
      tesseract-ocr tesseract-ocr-eng libimage-exiftool-perl

or run 'scripts/setup.sh --qt', which also installs what the tests use.
Qt 5 still works on older distributions: 'scripts/setup.sh --qt5' lists
its packages.

To build:

   cd paperman
   qmake6 paperman.pro -o Makefile
   make -f Makefile -j$(nproc) paperman

That makes 'paperman', which you can run in place:

   ./paperman

If the tree has been built before with another version of Qt (such as
Qt 5), run 'make distclean' first: otherwise the old object files are
linked into the new build and it fails with many undefined references.

A plain 'make' (through GNUmakefile) builds everything: the desktop
program, the server, the Android and iPhone app and the documentation,
which needs more tools; see doc/build.rst

To build with the tests and run them:

   qmake6 paperman.pro CONFIG+=test -o Makefile
   make -f Makefile -j$(nproc) paperman
   QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen ./paperman -t

For Windows and macOS, see README.md or doc/build.rst


Getting started
---------------

When paperman first starts it offers a place to keep your papers. To
add another, right-click in the left pane and choose 'Add repository',
then pick the directory holding your paper files.
